WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:07.400
Vector, you went through the trouble 
of calling us, so what do you want?

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.630
If it's something boring, you won't get off easy.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.460
Rejoice. Your friends have rejoiced.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:17.350
What?!

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:25.950
Gilag! Alit!

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.650
How are you guys...?

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.730
You used up all your powers in the human world,

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.310
so shouldn't you have to sleep for a long time to recover?

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.520
We just couldn't stay asleep
 seeing how pathetic you guys have been!

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:40.770
What did you say?!

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.330
Whoa there! We just got a couple of our friends back!

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.720
Show some gratitude!

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.310
Fly Burning!

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:55.650
I have come to report the information you've been waiting a long time for!

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.780
Huh?! You didn't call me!

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.210
I see...

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.480
So a Number is located within the ruins of this Spartan City...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.410
Yes! It is likely that Yuma Tsukumo is headed there as we speak!

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:10.430
What?!

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.330
Oh~! If you stare at me with those sharp eyes,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.200
...my face... my face starts itching...!

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.550
Meaning, if we wait at those ruins, they'll stumble right into us!

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.440
Then I'll go!

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.390
Yuma Tsukumo's <i>my prey</i>!

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.680
I swear I'm gonna pulverize him with my own hands!

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:09.620
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.670
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:20.130
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.680
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.560
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.900
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.110
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.990
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:45.620
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.700
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:57.170
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.630
According to the airship, the location for the ruins containing the next Number is here, Spartan City.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.510
It's a lot livelier here than the other places we've visited.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.970
"Alit the Silent Fighter:
 Reunion of the Passionate Duelists!"

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.300
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.980
There were so many cute clothes here 
that we sort of lost ourselves.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.310
Rio-<i>san</i>, I heard the pasta and pizza in Spartan City is delicious!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.190
Oh, yes! That sounds nice.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.860
C'mon, guys...

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.860
Kotori Burning!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.530
~Everyone's downtown exploring around~

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.030
~While I'm here watching the ship like a lonely clown~

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.160
Darnit! It's so lonesome!

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:58.380
But where should we search in this city for the ruins containing the Number?

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.970
That's true. We can't just search aimlessly...

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:02.970
Whoa!

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:04.390
What's wrong?!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.760
Did you find something?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.470
There! Look over there!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.350
<i>Spartan City Pro Duel Tournament!</i>

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.610
Gosh... You really have nothing in your head but Dueling...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.990
I don't mean <i>that</i>! I mean that Duelist!

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.280
<i>The mysterious Duelist, Gauche the Starman!</i>

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.200
Gauche the Starman?

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.450
<i>That's a good mood you're in!</i>

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.960
That guy's Gauche!

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.420
<i>Now, the cries echo throughout</i>

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.960
<i>as the gladiator wielding his Power Deck makes his entrance!</i>

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.720
<i>Oily Muscle!</i>

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.720
Oily!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.930
<i>He's facing the mysterious masked man descending like a shooting star!</i>

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.730
<i>Gauche the Starman!</i>

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.110
Gauche! Gauche! Gauche!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.360
<i>The messenger from the stars, Gauche the Starman!</i>

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.900
<i>He's super popular among the kids!</i>

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.200
Gauche! Gauche! Gauche!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.830
Hell yeah! That really lifts my mood!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.210
Gauche the Starman!

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:21.630
Take down Oily Muscle!

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.930
<i>Your star's about to fall!</i>

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.810
Go, Kusanagi! Direct Attack him!

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.270
<i>It's been decided! Gauche the Starman
 wins in an overwhelming victory!</i>

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.690
Gauche! Gauche! Gauche! Gauche!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.530
Next up's the battle for Champion!

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.950
You'll definitely win!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.080
Yup! You bet!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.990
Gimme your autograph!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.040
Gauche! Droite!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.670
You're... Yuma!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.750
Man did you surprise me!

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.130
I can't believe you became a Pro Duelist, Gauche!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.550
You're totally popular!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.340
Guess so. I'm the envoy of stardom, Gauche the Starman.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:13.560
I've won a bunch of challenges, and the next one's the fight for Champion.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.520
Are you also a Pro Duelist now, Droite-<i>san</i>?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.480
No, I'm this guy's manager.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.570
I tried to get her to debut with me as the Masked Tag Duelists pair, but she refused!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.150
You bet I did!

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.700
Rising!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.620
I-I get why...

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.160
Just a little tight...

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.120
But why dress as the messenger from the stars?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.210
I just wanted to show children a star of hope.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.880
The city me and Droite were born in was terrible.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.670
We did our best just to survive day-to-day.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.430
But Dueling was the one thing that shone through.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.180
A heated Duel that made you really excited...

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.640
It eventually made us start looking toward a dream.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.520
Before we knew it, that dream became our star of hope.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.320
No matter how dark the night sky may be, if there's at least one star visible,

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.570
you can live and head toward it.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.660
I want to show those tykes that star of hope.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.620
That's why I became the messenger from the stars, 
Gauche the Starman.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.960
Looks like I ran my mouth again.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.090
That's not true! That's a great dream!

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.010
Yeah.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.390
Gauche, I understand your dream all too well.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:38.930
Because I fought my hardest to save Haruto.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.850
Unlike a certain someone who doesn't cherish his baby sister.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.360
What'd you say?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.740
By the way, why did you guys come to this city?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.740
Actually, we're looking for some ruins.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:54.780
Ruins?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.130
Welcome.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.290
What can I get you?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.050
I want you to tell me where I can find ruins in this city.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.600
So your dad left clues about these ruins?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.430
Also, if there's any legend surrounding the ruins in this city...

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.190
If that's the case, there is one famous location.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.860
There's a legend about a gladiator's soul wandering the ruins of a Colosseum.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.190
What is that legend?

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:39.830
In this land, there was said to be a gladiator who won his way through this fists alone.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.000
And he had a rival.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.290
That was this country's prince.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.920
The gladiator and the prince
 fought each other time and time again,

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:55.050
Their fighting spirits forged a bond that surpassed their positions.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.350
Then one day, the two of them met for their final showdown.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.390
But letting the prince lose in front of 
such a large crowd was not allowed.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.560
The aids set the gladiator with a false crime and captured him.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.320
The prince pleaded desperately for his rival, the gladiator,

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.950
but they wouldn't listen to him, and then, in front of a large crowd,

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.870
the gladiator was cruelly executed.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.290
So cruel...

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.670
After a long period of time, that country was destroyed,

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:35.630
but the spirit of the gladiator is said to still wander the ruins of the Colosseum.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.850
I guess he still has a grudge for being executed on a false charge.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.550
That's not it.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.730
He still wants to fight.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.810
The regret he bore for not being
 able to finish his fight with his rival

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.150
has called his spirit back to the Colosseum.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:55.240
But those ruins are now submerged by a lake.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.490
Eh? The ruins sunk into a lake?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.200
It's over there.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.710
It's said that in order to seal the wandering spirit of the gladiator,

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.960
residents built a water bank in the location.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.920
Wha?! What'll we do?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:15.590
It's almost night.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.970
We'll figure the rest out tomorrow.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.300
<i>So the ruins are inside that lake...</i>

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.350
Looks like they still haven't realized it.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.360
Then I guess I'll mess it up a bit.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.570
<i>Next up's the battle for Champion!</i>

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.370
<i>You'll definitely win!</i>

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:51.790
Hmph! I can't believe I'm actually unable to sleep because of the pressure!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.840
What a terrible mood I'm in.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.840
"Those who obtain the soul of the gladiator are said

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.930
"to have unparalleled strength dwelling inside them," huh?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.020
To think I'd actually come here in the middle of the night believing that old story...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.480
Especially when these ruins are at the bottom of a lake to begin with.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.860
Trap, activate.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:21.820
What the?!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.710
Yuma! Yuma!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:37.880
What the heck?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.340
Something's going on at the lake.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.050
Just what's going on here?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.390
The water in the lake ran dry.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:47.140
Huh?

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:49.480
That's...

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.900
Are those the ruins containing the Number?

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.020
Most likely.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:55.940
Then those Barian guys...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.980
If they did, then the Number...

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.150
Ryouga...

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:01.990
But...

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.490
I feel really uneasy all of a sudden...

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:05.660
Rio...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.030
What's wrong?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.870
Did you find something?

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:16.340
No way! If I eat that much pasta, I'm gonna get fat!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.670
Just what the hec-

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.390
Wh-What the hell is this?!

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.510
The Colosseum appeared!

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.060
Sorry for bothering you in the middle of the night.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.520
Don't worry about it. You're in a hurry, right?

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:39.190
But where the heck did that darn Gauche run off to?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.920
<i>What is...this sensation?</i>

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.890
That's the Number...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.360
So you're the Number of these ruins?!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.900
Trying to resist me?!

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:31.910
They who lackith a heated fighting spirit shalt not absorb my soul!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:38.630
Dost thou havith the heated fighting spirit of thine who lovith fighting among thine heart?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.130
Yeah, I sure do!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:45.420
By that, I mean I've got the fighting spirit to beat Yuma Tsukumo's ass down!

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.600
Could you be...?!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:09.070
Wow... You sure are a powerful Number.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:15.200
But at the same time, it requires a huge risk for the Duelist using it...

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.330
Hey, you!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.830
What are you doing over there?

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:23.590
if I remember correctly, this guy's a Pro Duelist.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.170
Gauche?!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.140
Gauche... why are you here?!

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:34.810
Huh?

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.640
You're...

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.110
Alit!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.440
Tsukumo...

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.070
Yuma!

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.200
That's...

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.450
I've been really worried about you!

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.580
I've been worried, too!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:59.080
That you'd get beaten by someone else other than me!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.330
<i>So you can't wait to get into a fight, huh?</i>

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.960
<i>But you're far too zealous for me right now...</i>

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.970
Hey, Yuma, what kinda mood is in the air here?

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.510
Is this guy someone you know?

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.640
<i>That's it. If I use this knucklehead...</i>

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.190
You're named Gauche, right?
 I'll lend you this guy for a while!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.900
This is a... Number!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:30.110
Use that to help me beat down Yuma Tsukumo!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.210
A-Alit, you...!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:41.790
Gauche!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.420
Everything is for... the Barian World.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.800
Alit! Why'd you brainwash Gauche?!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:50.720
What did you say?

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.550
Who are you?!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:56.100
I'm Alit, a member of the Seven Barian Lords.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.850
Barian, you said?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.850
Weren't you destroyed along with the one with Dr. Faker?!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.560
We've finally got enough people.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.690
Let's treat ourself to a Tag Duel.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.320
A Tag Duel, you said?

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:11.820
We'll have to win the Duel if we want to free Gauche from his control!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.950
Okay, in that case, Yuma...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.120
I'll team with you as your partner.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.030
Eh?

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.370
I'm Gauche's manager.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:25.580
If his heart has fallen before an enemy, it's my job to get it back!

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:26.670
So let's do it!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.420
Yeah!

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.340
Wait! He's no ordinary person!

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:32.470
I'll...

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.130
Ryouga.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.550
Let Droite do this.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.640
C'mon, man. Try making a happier face!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:44.270
Haven't you been wanting to Duel against me again?!

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.230
Yeah, I have.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.690
I've wanted to have another 
heated Duel with you since that last time!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:56.200
But why would you go and involve Gauche in this too?!

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:57.910
Don't worry about it!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.870
I gave it a lot of thought before
 I decided to put this useless guy to work!

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.410
Useless?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.080
Our little chat ends here!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.090
Let's do it, then!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.260
Duel Disk, set!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:15.010
D-Gazer, set!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.510
Duel!!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:24.480
I'll go first. My turn! Draw!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:29.020
I'll Summon Heroic Challenger Ambush Soldier from my hand!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.780
I end my turn with this.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.820
Gauche...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.700
My turn! Draw!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:46.370
Alit... Why are you...? Why...?

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:52.000
Calm down, Yuma. You're letting anger mislead your judgment.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.970
I get it... I <i>get</i> it!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.340
I Summon Gagaga Magician from my hand!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.760
Gagaga!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.680
Then I activate the Continuous Magic, Gagaga Mirror!

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.190
When I have one Gagaga Monster on my field,

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.070
this card can be treated as Xyz Material with the same level!

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:17.950
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Mirror!

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.990
With these two Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.870
Xyz Summon!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.130
Come forth, Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.380
Hope!

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:37.800
Calling your Ace out from the start. <i>So</i> hotblooded.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.050
During their first turn, neither player can attack!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.930
I set one card and end my turn!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:51.100
This Duel will go on until a team is completely crushed.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.860
Here goes! My turn! Draw!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.110
I set one Monster face-down!

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.320
Then I set two cards and end my turn.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.660
My turn! Draw!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.540
I'll set one Monster face-down.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.130
Then I set two cards and end my turn.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:21.430
Somehow, that Alit person's aura is completely different from before!

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.520
My turn! Draw!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:31.230
From my hand, I Summon Heroic Challenger Clasp Knife!

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.940
Then Ambush Soldier's effect activates!

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:42.490
By releasing a Monster that stayed on my field for more than one turn,

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:48.870
I can change the levels of two Heroic Challengers in my hand to one and Special Summon them!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.080
Appear, Double Lance!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.750
Night Watchman!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:01.510
I Overlay the Level One Double Lance, Night Watchman, and Clasp Knife!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.890
With these three Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.760
Xyz Summon!

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:13.310
Come forth, Number 54!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:21.900
Your hot-blooded war cry will shake even sleeping souls!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.120
Rebellious Fighter - Lion Heart!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.710
So that's the Number from these ruins!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.210
It's got only 100 Attack Points!

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.330
But...

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.920
Lion Heart, while in Attack Position, cannot be destroyed by battle!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:45.340
With Lion Heart, I will attack Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.390
That’s suicide!

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.350
Are you trying to give yourself 2400 damage?!

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.770
Lion Heart's Monster Effect activates!

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:58.400
When this Monster battles, the damage that the player took...

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.400
...will also inflicted on the opposing player!

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:03.280
What?!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.070
Impossible!

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:07.950
Burning Cross Counter!

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:24.260
Gauche!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:25.590
Yuma!

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.310
He's aiming for a reckless simultaneous suicidal strategy?

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.140
That's right.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.140
But it's not me being reckless...

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.060
It's that knucklehead over there!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.570
Be crushed <i>bravely</i> alongside Yuma!

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.360
Alit! Just what has happened to you!?

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:49.370
You were a guy who would never have fought like <i>this</i>!

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:54.580
Yuma Tsukumo, the hatred I harbor from my loss to you is what changed me!

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.110
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:26.650
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:27.860
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.280
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:34.660
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:37.210
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:38.290
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:39.330
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.710
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.050
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:48.170
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.390
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:53.390
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.350
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:56.730
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:58.600
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:02.900
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:07.990
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.240
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:13.240
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:18.620
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:23.960
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:28.340
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:43.940
Alit took control of Gauche and started a Duel with us!

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:46.860
Because this ruin's Number works as a double-edged sword,

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:50.490
due to its effect, Gauche’s body has almost reached its limit!

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:52.990
Gauche is <i>not</i> a puppet!

00:23:53.110 --> 00:23:54.910
If the Duel goes on like this...

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.620
Cut it out, Alit!

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:59.290
All our fates lie in his hands!

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:02.000
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:05.000
"Be Revived! The Duelist Soul That Transcends Life!!"

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:08.000
I'll beat your soul clean!
